## Summary

      Completed a hands-on lab focused on identifying and analyzing potentially malicious activity on Windows and Linux systems. I used Task Manager, Resource Monitor, Process Explorer, top, and htop to monitor resource utilization and inspect running processes. I also configured Active Directory audit policies, simulated an unauthorized privilege escalation, and used Event Viewer to detect it through Event IDs 4728 and 4737. The lab reinforced the importance of baselining normal system behavior, enabling the right audit policies before an incident occurs, and reviewing security logs to spot signs of account compromise.
